   "status": "known_mismatch",
   "note": "Known mismatch: promethazine in Apr to May 2021 is below its own 95 to 110 range in every arm, including both controls (time trend, not radiation). The amoxicillin second analysis date is the sheet date; the file labels it 2019. Calibration anchor for the computed layer: the amoxicillin JSC control series (sealed capsule, three time points) is a measured trend the computed layer is calibrated against, so keep it out of any validation set used to judge that layer. Delivered doses 422.7 to 465.3 mGy and 864.4 to 932.4 mGy. Lots: acetaminophen Major NDC 00904-1988-60; amoxicillin Sandoz NDC 00781-2613-01, expiry 31 December 2019; ibuprofen Amneal NDC 65162-0464-10; promethazine Amneal NDC 65162-0521-10, expiry 29 February 2020. Storage at controlled room temperature with MKT within range. Promethazine in 2021 is below its own 95 to 110 range in every arm, including controls. Use: negative control for any radiation term; time trend for sealed and blister-packed products."
